  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre recorded $532M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 27 awards. General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre averaged $19.7M per award and obligations were down 9.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows variability, with obligations of $229M in FY21, $216M in FY22, $833M in FY23, $595M in FY24, $586M in FY25, and $532M in FY26. Market concentration is heavy: Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing accounts for $389M and Facilities Support Services accounts for $143M in FY2026 to date. The current-year totals are partial because fiscal year to date figures are not final. Use this information to prioritize outreach and proposal planning where Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing and Facilities Support Services matter most. The historical series highlights when award activity spiked and receded, which can guide resource allocation for capture and contract performance teams.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre obligations were $229M in FY21, $216M in FY22, $833M in FY23, $595M in FY24, $586M in FY25, and $532M in FY26. General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre obligations are down 9.2% year over year in FY2026 to date compared with the prior year. General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre saw the largest single-year total in FY23 at $833M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre revenue?",
        "body": "Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing is the largest market for General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre at $389M in FY2026 to date. Facilities Support Services is the second market at $143M in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Ots Wilkes Barre concentration in those two NAICS explains the majority of current-year obligations."
      }
    ]
